{
  "hypothesis": "Improve memory locality and loop order by reorganizing the loops to process points in a more cache-friendly manner. Specifically, we will focus on reducing the number of times distances are updated and sorted by using blocking techniques.",
  "transformations": [
    "Reordered the loops to process groups in blocks to improve cache locality.",
    "Reduced the frequency of sorting operations by maintaining a fixed-size list of nearest neighbors."
  ],
  "sources_kept": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/knn.c",
      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n\n#define BLOCK_SIZE 128\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float distance;\n    char label;\n} DistanceLabel;\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    DistanceLabel * nearest = (DistanceLabel *) malloc(sizeof(DistanceLabel) * k);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        nearest[i].distance = -1;\n        nearest[i].label = -1;\n    }\n\n    int group_start, group_end;\n    for (group_start = 0; group_start < n_groups; group_start += BLOCK_SIZE) {\n        group_end = group_start + BLOCK_SIZE;\n        if (group_end > n_groups) group_end = n_groups;\n\n        for (int i = group_start; i < group_end; i++) {\n            Group g = groups[i];\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n                float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n\n                int x;\n                for (x = k - 1; x >= 0 && (nearest[x].distance == -1 || d < nearest[x].distance); x--) {\n                    if (x + 1 < k) {\n                        nearest[x + 1] = nearest[x];\n                    }\n                }\n\n                if (x + 1 < k) {\n                    nearest[x + 1].distance = d;\n                    nearest[x + 1].label = g.label;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    char most_frequent = nearest[0].label;\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (nearest[i].label != nearest[i - 1].label) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = nearest[i - 1].label;\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n        most_frequent = nearest[k - 1].label;\n    }\n\n    free(nearest);\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/knn.h",
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float x;\n    float y;\n} Point;\n\ntypedef struct {\n    char label;\n    int length;\n    Point * points;\n} Group;\n\nvoid on_error() {\n    printf(\"Invalid input file.\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n}\n\nint parse_number_of_groups() {\n    int n;\n    if (scanf(\" n_groups=%d \", &n) != 1) on_error();\n\n    return n;\n}\n\nPoint parse_point() {\n    float x, y;\n    if (scanf(\" (%f ,%f) \", &x, &y) != 2)  on_error();\n\n    Point point;\n    point.x = x;\n    point.y = y;\n\n    return point;\n}\n\nGroup parse_next_group() {\n    char label; \n    int length;\n\n    if (scanf(\" label=%c \", &label) != 1) on_error();\n    if (scanf(\" length=%d \", &length) != 1) on_error();\n\n    Group group;\n    group.label = label;\n    group.length = length;\n    group.points = (Point *) malloc(sizeof(Point) * length);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < length; i++) {\n        group.points[i] = parse_point();\n    }\n\n    return group;\n}\n\nint parse_k() {\n    int k;\n    if (scanf(\" k=%d \", &k) != 1) on_error();\n\n    return k;\n}\n\nfloat euclidean_distance_no_sqrt (Point a, Point b) {\n    return ((b.x - a.x) * ((b.x - a.x))) + ((b.y - a.y) * (b.y - a.y));\n}"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Reorganized the loops to process groups in blocks to improve cache locality and reduced the frequency of sorting operations by maintaining a fixed-size list of nearest neighbors."
}
